"""A context-sensitive zero detector.

Leading zeroes, zero fractional parts, and zeroes in identifiers are stronger
than zeroes inside ordinary integers. Null/nil comparisons, subscript and
split Arabic digits, LaTeX environment boundaries, and line-initial 1 are
secondary cues. Numeric amplitudes are calibrated on training examples, not exact rules
of arithmetic. State resets at document boundaries.
