Negative poles include business/camp (营), recording (录), drinking (饮),
copying (抄), pouring (灌), cooking (煎), and several Korean syllables.
Quotation and maintenance words have smaller rules. A document-initial
run of middle dots has a positive response. Script and code-marker rules
give a coarse document-initial background. Split UTF-8 characters are
recognized when their last byte arrives. Ordinary text stays near zero.
"""
import unicodedata

READS = ()


def step(carry, prefix, upstream):
    doc = prefix.document_ids[-1]
    first = carry is None or carry[0] != doc
    if first:
        tail, before, only_dots = b'', '', True
    else:
        _, tail, before, only_dots = carry
